# Active engine plan

## P0 — Gemini transport recovery without wrapper interference

- [x] Remove Agent-specific retry-warning logic; the Agent consumes completed provider Content and uses each provider's own GenerateStream implementation.
- [x] Gemini retries recoverable transport interruptions after partial output, suppresses the exact replayed visible prefix, and streams only the new suffix.
- [x] Keep ordinary non-retried SSE Part boundaries unchanged; normalize text parts only after a successful replay.
- [x] Accept cleanly completed text responses from Gemini-compatible endpoints when finishReason is omitted.
- [x] Keep retry attempts bounded and make retry backoff and response parsing honor request cancellation.
- [x] Verify non-Gemini providers keep their native GenerateStream paths: OpenAI OAuth and OpenAI-compatible clients each implement GenerateStream independently of Gemini retry handling.
- [x] Add Agent regression coverage proving streamed text is presentation-only and completed function-call Content still executes once, with its response passed to the follow-up generation.
- [x] Run gofmt, shell syntax/completion tests, go test ./..., go vet ./..., and the Linux amd64 build on the latest work head. GitHub Actions run 44645204014 passed on 80ddb4b579955e49c8d250add9ea9268bfce8730.
- [ ] EXTERNAL VALIDATION BLOCKED: run live Gemini streaming smoke tests (long response, interrupted partial response, tool/function call, and final answer). CI has no Gemini API credential configured, and the connected local runner is offline. Mocked transport tests cover replay, duplicate suppression, backoff cancellation, malformed SSE, response parsing cancellation, and function-call handling; these are not a substitute for a real-provider smoke test.

## P0 — Request lifecycle and session isolation

- [x] Track each logical run with a generation and cancellable context. Reject stale model responses, tool calls, stream callbacks, context appends, history writes, and events.
- [x] /clear and /new cancel active work, pending approvals, shell subprocesses and teamwork operations; wait for the old run to stop before replacing history or accepting another request. Report a specific timeout if an operation does not stop.
- [x] Invalidate queued UI completion events so a prior request cannot finish or overwrite a newer request after a clear.
- [x] Propagate request context through Workspace file operations, shell approval, tool dispatch, and teamwork coordination. A late approval cannot authorize a mutation after cancellation.
- [x] Ensure Ctrl+C cancellation reaches Gemini streaming, retry backoff, response parsing, approvals, and shell process groups; report operations still active after the shutdown warning interval.
- [x] Scope repository instructions to repository-maintenance prompts. Explicit no-tools prompts do not load workspace guidance, expose tool schemas, or execute unexpected tool calls.
- [x] Add regressions for clear during generation, stale stream callback, pending approval, running shell, stale UI completion, and a fresh explicit no-tools request after session clear.

## P0 — TUI incremental rendering and menu-navigation flicker

- [ ] Fix the Go TUI renderer so menu navigation does not clear and redraw the entire screen. Cursor movement, selection changes, submenu open/close, and other local interactions must update only the affected rows/cells or components.
- [ ] Preserve unchanged panels and their screen contents; avoid full-screen repaint, clear-screen sequences, and cursor jumps during ordinary menu navigation.
- [ ] Keep rendering incremental while model streaming, tool output, status-line updates, and interactive menus are active; UI updates must not interrupt or disable streaming.
- [ ] Add regression tests for menu cursor movement, selection changes, submenu transitions, and concurrent streaming/status updates. Verify emitted terminal output contains only the necessary changed regions rather than a full-screen redraw.
- [ ] Manually verify on a real terminal that repeated up/down navigation and opening/closing menus produce no visible flicker.

